[TEXT] **Critical finding — dswa1 has TWO rules in the FORWARD chain (infra_sweep only showed the drop rule):**

```
iifname "br0.10" meta l4proto icmp  ip saddr 10.1.0.0/24 ip daddr 10.3.0.0/24  → ACCEPT (6 pkts / 504 bytes matched)
iifname "br0.10"                    ip saddr 10.1.0.0/24 ip daddr 10.3.0.0/24  → DROP   (0 pkts)
```

**This is the real fault:** ICMP (ping) from 10.1.0.0/24 → 10.3.0.0/24 is explicitly allowed; **all other protocols (TCP/UDP) are silently dropped.** The reachability tests only use ICMP, which is why they showed 0% loss — the TCP drop is invisible to ping-based probes.

This is an ACL-family fault. → **Phase 3: entering ACL skill.**
